{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/7/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"64efde09\" lines=\"68-83\">\n<description>\nCopy colored control-ray ports from one rectangular sprite orientation to every matching transformed sprite.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg is the most common color.\n- Several dense 2-by-N or N-by-2 rectangular sprites are dihedral transforms of one template.\n- Isolated single-pixel control markers sit on rays projected outward from the dominant long edge of some sprites.\n\nRule:\n- For each sprite, the active edge is the long side whose cells have the strongest same-color majority.\n- A control marker seen first along an outward ray from an active-edge cell assigns its color to that template cell.\n- On every transformed sprite, draw that assigned color outward from the corresponding active-edge cell through bg cells until blocked or out of bounds.\n\nKey insight:\n- The marker positions are not absolute; they label cells of a shared rectangular template, then the labels follow each sprite's rotation/reflection.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"bd5af378\" lines=\"25-42\">\n<description>\nRewrite a corner L block into two nested L borders and a diagonal trace.\n\nInput structure\nA rectangular grid has exactly two colors: one color forms a one-cell-thick\nL on two adjacent outer edges, and the other color fills the remaining\nrectangle.\n\nRule\nNormalize the L to the top-left corner. Paint the outer top-left L with the\nfill color, the next inner L with the original border color, and the main\ndiagonal of the remaining inner rectangle with the fill color. All other\ncells become color 8, then the original orientation is restored.\n\nKey insight\nThe corner of the input L determines the orientation; after flipping to a\ncanonical top-left L, the output is the same nested-layer pattern for every\nexample.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"cf5fd0ad\" lines=\"10-22\">\n<description>\nBuild a four-quadrant rotational tiling of the input square.\n\nInput structure\n- The input is a square grid treated as one complete sprite.\n\nRule\n- Each output quadrant is a 2x2 repetition of a rotated copy of the whole input.\n- The quadrant rotations are upper-left 180 degrees, upper-right 90 degrees\n  clockwise, lower-left 90 degrees counterclockwise, and lower-right unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The output is a 4x4 grid of original-size blocks, not a per-pixel scale-up.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"52df9849\" lines=\"49-67\">\n<description>\nComplete each partially hidden simple foreground shape by recoloring the occluding pixels in its footprint.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background and several solid foreground shapes.\n- Some shapes are partially hidden by other foreground colors, but their full\n  footprint is still indicated by a foreground-filled bbox or by a foreground-\n  filled 45-degree diagonal line.\n\nRule\n- For each foreground color, complete its full rectangular bbox when that bbox\n  contains no background and includes other colors.\n- Otherwise, complete its 45-degree diagonal line when all visible pixels lie\n  on that line and the hidden line cells are foreground, not background.\n- Recolor only those hidden footprint pixels; leave all other pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The occluded cells are exactly the non-background cells inside a simple\n  shape's implied footprint, so completing shapes is a local recoloring problem.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"d8e07eb2\" lines=\"29-47\">\n<description>\nLook up query glyphs in a reference table and mark whether they form a line.\n\nInput structure:\n- Teal background with two full-width pink separator rows.\n- Above the first separator is a query row of 5x5 glyph cells.\n- Between separators is a reference table of the same 5x5 cells; a glyph is\n  identified by both its color and its 3x3 shape.\n\nRule:\n- Green-fill the background inside every table cell whose glyph exactly\n  appears in the query row.\n- If the matched table cells form one complete row or one complete column,\n  also green-fill the query band and the bottom verdict band.\n- Otherwise leave the query band unchanged and fill the bottom verdict band red.\n\nKey insight: The bottom color is not a count; it is the yes/no answer to\nwhether the queried glyphs align as a full row or column in the table.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"fbf15a0b\" lines=\"49-69\">\n<description>\nCrop out the grid half containing the two aligned marker pixels, then erase the markers to background.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background color and one non-background marker color\n  that appears as exactly two cells.\n- The marker cells are aligned either in one row or one column and both lie\n  in the same half along that direction.\n- Other non-background pixels are content inside one or both halves.\n\nRule\n- If the markers share a row, keep the left or right half whose columns\n  contain them.\n- If the markers share a column, keep the top or bottom half whose rows\n  contain them.\n- In the kept half, recolor the marker pixels to the background color.\n\nKey insight\n- The two marker pixels are not part of the picture; their alignment and\n  half-position identify which half of the doubled canvas is the answer.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d749d46f\" lines=\"32-51\">\n<description>\nPack each solid foreground rectangle twice: wide across the top and tall from the bottom.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has one background color and one foreground color; the foreground forms\nseparate solid rectangles, ordered from left to right.\n\nRule\nBuild a 10-row background canvas whose width is the packed width of the wide\nversions of the rectangles. For each source rectangle, paint a top-aligned\nrectangle of shape min(h,w) by max(h,w), with one background column between\nconsecutive rectangles. Then, starting again from the left edge, paint a\nbottom-aligned rectangle of shape max(h,w) by min(h,w) for each source rectangle,\nagain separated by one background column.\n\nKey insight\nThe input rectangles are not copied in their original orientations; each object\ncontributes one horizontal-facing and one vertical-facing normalized rectangle,\npreserving left-to-right object order.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a644e277\" lines=\"31-50\">\n<description>\nExtract the lattice subregion bounded by the four background-colored corner holes.\n\nInput structure:\n- A regular one-cell-thick lattice has one line color, one background color,\n  and sparse marker pixels.\n- Exactly four lattice-line intersections are background-colored holes instead\n  of line-color pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Find the unique non-background color that forms regular horizontal and\n  vertical lattice lines.\n- Use the four background-colored lattice intersections as the corners of one\n  rectangle.\n- Return the inclusive crop between those corner rows and columns.\n\nKey insight:\n- The crop is marked by the missing lattice intersections, not by the marker\n  pixels inside the cells.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"538b439f\" lines=\"122-142\">\n<description>\nReflect the solid rectangular source objects across the full separator line and color the gap with the separator color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one full-width or full-height one-pixel\n  separator line in a non-background color.\n- One other foreground color forms solid rectangular objects, all strictly on the same side of that separator.\n- Remaining non-background pixels are scattered distractors.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the input grid shape and unchanged pixels outside each affected corridor.\n- Mirror each source object across the separator line.\n- For every source object, recolor the rectangular strip between the\n  original object and its reflection to the separator color, then paint the\n  reflected object in the source color.\n\nKey insight:\n- The full straight line is a mirror axis; the real objects are identified\n  structurally as the only solid rectangles confined to one side, while\n  scattered pixels are noise that may be overwritten inside the corridor.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a834deea\" lines=\"20-39\">\n<description>\nFill each black 5x5 region's missing interior positions with a fixed 3x3 positional color legend.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid uses teal as the dominant background and black for one or more\n  5x5 regions.\n- Each black region has a black one-pixel border and a 3x3 interior that\n  may already contain teal pixels.\n\nRule\n- Overlay the legend 1 7 6 / 4 8 5 / 2 9 3 on the 3x3 interior of every\n  5x5 black region.\n- Wherever an interior non-center legend position is still black, recolor it\n  to the corresponding legend color; leave existing teal pixels, the center,\n  and the black border unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The colored output pixels are not derived from the teal motif shape; they\n  are the fixed position labels for the missing cells of each 3x3 interior.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e3f79277\" lines=\"8-23\">\n<description>\nReplace a corner L with a same-color right-triangle outline in the corresponding corner of an enlarged canvas.\n\nInput structure:\n- The input is a square grid with one background color and one foreground color.\n- The foreground is a one-pixel-thick L inside a square bbox.\n- The L touches exactly one horizontal grid edge and one vertical grid edge, identifying a corner.\n\nRule:\n- Fill a square output canvas of side 3n-2, where n is the input side length, with the background color.\n- Double the L leg length to get the triangle side length.\n- Draw the two perpendicular triangle legs on the same output corner edges and connect their free endpoints with the diagonal.\n\nKey insight:\n- The input L encodes the corner, color, and side length of the triangle outline; the missing side is the diagonal between the L's two free endpoints.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9473c6fb\" lines=\"10-25\">\n<description>\nRecolor the sparse foreground pixels in scan order along their longer spread, cycling red, teal, and grey.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- Every foreground object is a single isolated 4-connected pixel.\n- The foreground pixel set has a rectangular bbox whose row or column extent defines the scan direction.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the background unchanged.\n- If the foreground bbox is at least as tall as it is wide, order foreground pixels row-major; otherwise order them column-major.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"实现思路已定：\n\n1. 用非黑像素的 4 连通分量找每个窗户，再从其 bbox 内定位唯一的整条 Grey 行和整条 Grey 列，得到十字交叉点与四个象限尺寸。\n2. 以面积最小象限为目标象限，对四个象限分别取“靠近十字线”的可见子块，按需要做水平/垂直翻折，统计每个落点叠了几层 Yellow，生成压缩后的左上角小矩形。\n3. 生成器随机化窗户数量、位置、尺寸、十字偏移方向、标记分布与颜色，并且用 `main()` 做 oracle 校验，只接受满足尺寸、非重叠、方向唯一、输出正确的样例。"}}
